# Cursor Rules for PoolAI Project

## Documentation Structure

- All `.md` files should be created in `docs/` directory with appropriate subdirectories
- Keep root directory clean - only `README.md` and `README.uk.md` should be in root
- Use the following structure:
  - `docs/status/` - Current status and stable state documents
  - `docs/development/` - Development plans and roadmaps
  - `docs/archive/` - Historical/archived documents
  - `docs/concept/` - Concept files
  - `docs/deployment/` - Deployment guides
  - `docs/configuration/` - Configuration guides
  - `docs/monitoring/` - Monitoring setup guides
  - `docs/security/` - Security documentation
  - `docs/performance/` - Performance tuning guides
  - `docs/troubleshooting/` - Troubleshooting guides
  - `docs/migration/` - Migration guides
  - `docs/vm/` - VM module documentation

## File References

- When referencing documentation files, use relative paths from the file location
- Example: `[Current Status](../status/CURRENT_STATUS.md)`
- Always update links when moving files

## Git Workflow

- Commit documentation changes with descriptive messages
- Use conventional commit format: `docs: organize documentation structure`
- Keep commits focused on documentation organization

## Rust Code References

- When referencing concept files in Rust code comments, use: `docs/concept/poolAI_concept.txt`
- Update all references when moving files

